# Example: Qwen3.8-27B Uncensored (abliterated) — multimodal (text + vision).
# VERIFIED WORKING: loads on one 80GB card (~32GB VRAM at 64K ctx), text + vision
# both confirmed through the webp proxy.
#
# Note the GGUF declares `general.architecture = qwen35` (Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration)
# despite the "3.8" name — so any llama.cpp with qwen35 support runs it; check with
#   grep -oE '"qwen3[^"]*"' ~/llama.cpp/src/llama-arch.cpp
#
# The `noMTP` quant is chosen deliberately: the repo also ships MTP-fused files, but
# the MTP block is inert on a normal forward pass and the model card reports identical
# PPL, so noMTP removes a compatibility variable for no quality cost.
REPO=JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
MODEL_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-noMTP-Q8_0.gguf
MMPROJ_FILE=mmproj-Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-F16.gguf
ALIAS=qwen3.8-27b
MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/qwen3.8-27b-uncensored

GPU=0
SPORT=8080       # bump these (e.g. 8082/8083) to run alongside another model
PPORT=8081
NGL=999

CTX_SIZE=65536   # native context is 262144; 64K keeps the KV cache sane
REASONING_BUDGET=-1
REASONING=true
MAXTOKENS=32768

# Qwen3 thinking-mode recommended sampling
TEMP=0.6
TOP_P=0.95
TOP_K=20

CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-12.6
CUDA_ARCHS="80;90"
CONDA_ENV=gguf
